export const rootSixOpening = {
  coreQuestion: 'What could threaten what I have built, and which tools reduce, transfer, contain, or prepare for that risk?',
  story: [
    'The last bridge ends at a stone checkpoint above the Harbor District. Behind Ivy and Eli, the Bridge District still glows with promises that brought tomorrow’s income into today. Ahead, the harbor holds what those crossings helped people build: homes, paychecks, records, businesses, health, family responsibilities, and choices.',
    'The protected water looks calm. Beyond the breakwater, a storm turns the open sea white. Ivy studies the wall and feels relieved. Eli studies the same wall and asks what happens if it fails. Sage points to the lighthouse, the marked channels, the gates, the watch stations, and the evacuation paths. No single structure protects the entire harbor.',
    '“Protection is not a promise that nothing will happen,” Sage tells them. “It is the work of deciding what matters, what could interrupt it, which risks you can reduce, which you can transfer, which you will carry, and what must still be ready if the first protection does not hold.”',
  ],
  promise: 'Root Six teaches protection without selling fear. The learner will practice seeing risk, reading coverage, securing identity and accounts, clarifying authority, recognizing exploitation, checking professionals, preserving evidence, and building a personal protection map. RootWise will not prescribe a policy, product, legal document, provider, or universal risk tolerance.',
};

